1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,348
Your crew has spent this whole class on the bridge.

2
00:00:06,148 --> 00:00:07,887
Today they get up,

3
00:00:08,337 --> 00:00:11,380
and they leave the ship, twice over.

4
00:00:13,180 --> 00:00:17,093
Once into a place made of rooms and choices.

5
00:00:17,993 --> 00:00:21,472
And once onto a map they walk across.

6
00:00:23,272 --> 00:00:28,054
And both of them hang on one line of a landmark.

7
00:00:29,254 --> 00:00:33,167
Here's a station, like the ones you've written before.

8
00:00:34,067 --> 00:00:36,241
It's in the home system,

9
00:00:36,691 --> 00:00:39,300
so nobody has to fly anywhere.

10
00:00:41,100 --> 00:00:43,709
And it has one new line.

11
00:00:44,159 --> 00:00:45,898
Site, and a key.

12
00:00:47,698 --> 00:00:52,046
That line says the crew can leave the ship here.

13
00:00:52,946 --> 00:00:56,859
And the key is the name of a file.

14
00:00:57,309 --> 00:00:59,483
Customs, dot a m d.

15
00:01:00,683 --> 00:01:02,857
So I make that file,

16
00:01:03,307 --> 00:01:06,350
and the whole place goes in it.

17
00:01:08,150 --> 00:01:10,759
It has three chapters in it.

18
00:01:11,659 --> 00:01:13,398
Voices says who's talking.

19
00:01:14,298 --> 00:01:18,211
Hails is the call that comes when we dock.

20
00:01:20,011 --> 00:01:21,750
Look at this answer.

21
00:01:22,650 --> 00:01:27,433
After it comes a semicolon, the word signal, and boarding down.

22
00:01:28,333 --> 00:01:30,507
That's the game's own word,

23
00:01:30,957 --> 00:01:33,565
and it's what sends a party.

24
00:01:35,365 --> 00:01:37,104
Then come the rooms,

25
00:01:37,554 --> 00:01:41,033
and the first one is where they arrive.

26
00:01:41,933 --> 00:01:44,541
Every room has a way back,

27
00:01:44,991 --> 00:01:48,035
and every room has a way home.

28
00:01:49,235 --> 00:01:52,278
Two more things on this one answer.

29
00:01:54,078 --> 00:01:56,687
The first is learn the manifest.

30
00:01:57,587 --> 00:02:00,196
Now the party knows a fact,

31
00:02:00,646 --> 00:02:02,820
and the place keeps it.

32
00:02:03,720 --> 00:02:07,633
This line is only spoken before they know it,

33
00:02:08,083 --> 00:02:10,257
and this one only after.

34
00:02:12,057 --> 00:02:14,230
And then signal, manifest read.

35
00:02:15,130 --> 00:02:16,870
That word is mine.

36
00:02:17,770 --> 00:02:22,552
Over in the universe file, I add a step of story

37
00:02:23,002 --> 00:02:26,480
that's done when it hears that same word.

38
00:02:28,280 --> 00:02:31,324
That's how a place finishes a step.

39
00:02:32,524 --> 00:02:34,698
Lint has six warnings now.

40
00:02:35,598 --> 00:02:38,641
Three are old friends from last time.

41
00:02:40,441 --> 00:02:44,789
The three new ones are wrong in the same way.

42
00:02:45,689 --> 00:02:49,602
Lint can't see the game listening for boarding down,

43
00:02:50,052 --> 00:02:53,965
and it doesn't join a signal across two files.

44
00:02:54,865 --> 00:02:58,343
So I count them, and I keep them.

45
00:03:00,143 --> 00:03:02,317
Now let's dock with it.

46
00:03:03,217 --> 00:03:06,696
A call comes in from the Customs House.

47
00:03:07,596 --> 00:03:10,204
Comms answers, and sends a party.

48
00:03:11,104 --> 00:03:12,843
And here's the counter.

49
00:03:14,643 --> 00:03:16,383
I read the manifest,

50
00:03:16,833 --> 00:03:19,876
and the step is done and paid.

51
00:03:20,776 --> 00:03:22,515
Back at the counter,

52
00:03:22,965 --> 00:03:26,878
the clerk has a different line for me now.

53
00:03:28,078 --> 00:03:32,426
Now the second place, and here's the rule for it.

54
00:03:33,326 --> 00:03:35,065
Say it with me.

55
00:03:36,865 --> 00:03:39,474
The landmark says site, tally yard.

56
00:03:40,374 --> 00:03:43,852
The map's first line says area, tally yard.

57
00:03:44,752 --> 00:03:46,491
It's the same key,

58
00:03:46,941 --> 00:03:49,115
and nothing else joins them.

59
00:03:50,915 --> 00:03:52,654
A map needs pictures,

60
00:03:53,104 --> 00:03:56,148
and they come in two art packs.

61
00:03:57,048 --> 00:04:00,961
So I add two lines to story dot json,

62
00:04:01,411 --> 00:04:03,585
and I watch my commas.

63
00:04:04,485 --> 00:04:08,398
One line at the end of the settings file.

64
00:04:09,298 --> 00:04:11,907
And then I fetch them, once.

65
00:04:13,107 --> 00:04:15,715
I'm handing you this map finished,

66
00:04:16,165 --> 00:04:20,078
because drawing one is a class of its own.

67
00:04:21,878 --> 00:04:24,052
Read it as a picture.

68
00:04:24,952 --> 00:04:27,996
There's a landing pad on the left,

69
00:04:28,446 --> 00:04:31,489
and a walled house with one door.

70
00:04:33,289 --> 00:04:36,767
And there's the first line, area, tally yard.

71
00:04:38,567 --> 00:04:40,741
Then the site's own file.

72
00:04:41,641 --> 00:04:44,685
It has the same call as before.

73
00:04:45,585 --> 00:04:48,628
And then what stands on the map.

74
00:04:49,078 --> 00:04:52,557
A door, a keycard, a terminal, a ledger.

75
00:04:53,457 --> 00:04:56,065
A calm man to talk to,

76
00:04:56,515 --> 00:04:58,689
and a loader that attacks.

77
00:05:00,489 --> 00:05:03,533
Every key starts with the word yard.

78
00:05:04,433 --> 00:05:09,215
Keep to that, and two places can never share a key.

79
00:05:10,415 --> 00:05:13,459
One more landmark, with its one line.

80
00:05:14,359 --> 00:05:16,533
One more step of story,

81
00:05:16,983 --> 00:05:19,157
opened by the first one.

82
00:05:20,957 --> 00:05:22,696
And lint says nine.

83
00:05:23,596 --> 00:05:25,770
That's two for the calls,

84
00:05:26,220 --> 00:05:28,393
four for the two steps,

85
00:05:28,843 --> 00:05:31,017
and the three old ones.

86
00:05:32,817 --> 00:05:34,557
Nine is today's clean.

87
00:05:35,457 --> 00:05:38,935
If you see a tenth, that one's real.

88
00:05:40,135 --> 00:05:42,743
So we dock with the yard,

89
00:05:43,193 --> 00:05:44,933
and the call comes.

90
00:05:45,833 --> 00:05:48,007
I go down from Weapons,

91
00:05:48,457 --> 00:05:51,065
and the side story is mine.

92
00:05:52,865 --> 00:05:55,474
First I deal with the loader.

93
00:05:56,374 --> 00:05:58,548
Then I try the door,

94
00:05:58,998 --> 00:06:00,737
and it stays shut.

95
00:06:01,637 --> 00:06:04,680
The keycard's lying out in the yard.

96
00:06:05,580 --> 00:06:09,493
I pick it up, and now the door opens.

97
00:06:11,293 --> 00:06:13,033
Inside there's the ledger.

98
00:06:13,933 --> 00:06:18,715
I close it, and the short count is done and paid.

99
00:06:20,515 --> 00:06:23,993
And when the last of us beams up,

100
00:06:24,443 --> 00:06:26,183
the visit is over.

101
00:06:27,383 --> 00:06:30,861
Now I dock again, and go back down.

102
00:06:31,761 --> 00:06:33,500
The door's still open,

103
00:06:33,950 --> 00:06:36,124
and the loader's still down.

104
00:06:37,924 --> 00:06:41,402
I leave the system, and I come back.

105
00:06:42,302 --> 00:06:44,911
The game built that station new,

106
00:06:45,361 --> 00:06:49,274
and the yard is just as I left it.

107
00:06:51,074 --> 00:06:54,117
Then I close the game, and continue.

108
00:06:54,567 --> 00:06:56,307
It's the same again.

109
00:06:58,107 --> 00:07:01,150
And here it is in the save.

110
00:07:01,600 --> 00:07:04,209
The door, the keycard, the loader,

111
00:07:04,659 --> 00:07:07,702
and what we learned in each place.

112
00:07:08,902 --> 00:07:11,511
Two honest words before you go.

113
00:07:13,311 --> 00:07:18,093
When I checked this page, a script did all of it,

114
00:07:18,543 --> 00:07:21,152
and nobody was watching a screen.

115
00:07:22,952 --> 00:07:25,996
And always give a site a call.

116
00:07:26,896 --> 00:07:31,243
A place with no call opens the moment you dock,

117
00:07:31,693 --> 00:07:35,172
and that can leave a visit hanging open.

118
00:07:36,072 --> 00:07:39,550
It's on the page, with the way out.

119
00:07:41,350 --> 00:07:43,089
Now it's your turn.

120
00:07:43,989 --> 00:07:45,728
Rename the customs house,

121
00:07:46,178 --> 00:07:48,787
and give it a fifth room.

122
00:07:49,687 --> 00:07:53,600
Then walk the yard as far as the ledger.
